    method_title: 'Method and credits',
    m_data_pipe: 'This site shows current data only: {p} GH1 structures from the PDB and {r} residues. They were chosen with InterPro IPR001360, at 3 Å or better, without catalytic mutants, and grouped at 90 % identity. Positions use the numbering of Pfam 32.0, so position 333 stays 333. 3SCU, a catalytic mutant, gives the frame of the substrate and is not in the set. Family core uses {c} positions.',
    m_replica: 'The new pipeline first had to reproduce 2020. It does: median error of {e} Å in distance over {p} pairs from {n} proteins, with local alignment and the HMM of Pfam 32.0. That model is inferred, from a {m} % match in numbering; it is not the original file.',
    m_frame: 'Frame of reference: origin on the anomeric carbon of the −1 sugar, y axis towards the glycosidic oxygen, x axis towards the projection of C4. θ runs from +y, φ is atan2(z, x). Maps show the view from the centre: north runs anticlockwise, south clockwise, φ = 0 at the top.',
    m_claim: 'EASiMap does not claim to be new science. Mapping proteins onto spheres and flat charts has a history, listed here. It offers one way of looking at a family, from the sugar outwards.',
